From 7bce495bf6eb9e5977ebc397db0a780a2cd75c3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:00:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(outcome): a silent unterminated subagent is lost, not
 gone: no derived done (false green) [daveey]

A delegate child whose session row never ended dropped out of the parent's
waits once its last activity passed SUBAGENT_LIVE_WINDOW_S (6 h). A later
closing-looking reply then derived `done` and painted the chat green while
the delegated work was unfinished (defect desktop-5a35611881: child
20261111_094134_4755e7 went silent at 10:06Z, parent derived done at 17:21Z).

Such a child is now *lost*: when it started within SUBAGENT_LOST_BOUND_S
(7 d) and was active after the chat's latest declared outcome, the outcome is
`unresolved{reason: subagent_lost, on: [{kind: subagent, state: lost}]}`.
It ranks after open decisions, lost requests and live waits (like
subagent_killed), and ahead of a declared wait or done made before it went
silent, so it is never done and never a wait that cannot end. A declared
outcome made after its last activity accounts for it; derived outcomes keep
`last_declared_at` so that accounting survives the declaration lapsing. An
unfinished-delegation note at the tail keeps its subagent_killed reason.

Desktop: reason type and tooltip copy for subagent_lost.
